Device Readiness & Audit System - Implementation Steps
This document outlines the four essential steps for building a device readiness evaluation and AI integration system using Hexagonal Architecture.

1. Define pilot device/workload, approved sources, first profile schema and deterministic readiness concept
Purpose: Define data characteristics, design validation schemas using Zod, and build the deterministic core evaluation logic independently of external factors.

Associated File: domain/deviceEvaluator.js

2. Finalize structured device/benchmark fields and test readiness inputs/outputs
Purpose: Build foundational interfaces and contracts (Ports) that dictate how the system communicates with data sources and AI services in an organized and stable manner.

Associated Files: ports/deviceRepository.js and ports/aiServicePort.js

3. Integrate official evidence and readiness tool with benchmark API/UI: verify not-measured and conflict behavior
Purpose: Implement actual adapters (Adapters) to fetch the 8 official devices, validate them using Zod, connect the system to local Ollama for intelligent insights, and handle Conflict and Not-Measured states.

Associated Files: adapters/jsonDeviceRepository.js and adapters/ollamaServiceAdapter.js

4. Audit production recommendations, regression cases, limitations and documentation against rubric
Purpose: Serve as the main execution entry point and orchestrator (Primary Adapter), bringing all layers together to produce final reports and audits verifying device readiness.

Associated File: app.js
